<title>UK: UK Labour to consider extending TESSAS, PEPS - Brown.</title>
<headline>UK Labour to consider extending TESSAS, PEPS - Brown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British Labour government would consider extending the principle of tax-exempt savings and investment accounts such as TESSAs and PEPs, economics spokesman Gordon Brown said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said he would consult when in government on a proposal to to introduce a new Individual Savings Account (ISA).</p>
<p>Making a keynote speech on public finance, Brown said that in the case of ISAs, &quot;tax relief would be geared to encouraging savers to invest in the long term, with relief becoming available and payable after a period of years.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
